#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:9
msgid ""
"Spiral is a GTK4 and libadwaita file manager for Wayland desktops that come "
"without one. It follows the layout and behaviour of GNOME Files and adds a "
"file chooser portal backend, so applications that open and save files "
"through the portal get the same picker."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:11
msgid ""
"Grid, list and column views, tabs, and a places sidebar with devices, "
"bookmarks and favorites"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:12
msgid ""
"Copy, move, trash, rename and duplicate with progress, conflict handling and "
"undo"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:13
msgid "Archive extraction and creation with the tools installed on the system"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:14
msgid "Sandboxed thumbnails, drag and drop, and \"Open in Terminal\""
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:15
msgid ""
"The org.freedesktop.FileManager1 service, so browsers and chat apps can show "
"a file in its folder"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:22
msgid "sachesi"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:27
msgid ""
"Column view no longer decides the view of every folder after it: a folder "
"that remembers a view of its own gets it back, while columns still survive a "
"move that has nothing else to say. Where the system cannot keep a setting "
"with each folder, that choice now falls to the global default instead of "
"going nowhere at all, and the preference says as much. Opening a window or a "
"tab no longer writes the zoom settings back over themselves, and the program "
"is half the size it was."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:32
msgid ""
"A quick preview on the Space key: images, PDFs a page at a time, video, "
"sound and text with source code among it, drawn by Spiral itself in a window "
"that takes the proportions of what it holds before it opens rather than "
"resizing in front of you. The arrows walk the folder without leaving the "
"preview, Page Up and Page Down turn the pages of a PDF, Return hands the "
"file to its application, and Ctrl with the wheel zooms a picture around the "
"pointer, which is then moved by dragging it. Video and sound play through "
"one GStreamer pipeline kept for the whole session, and a sound file shows "
"the cover it carries whether or not a thumbnailer ever saw it. A middle "
"click opens a folder in a new tab, the first arrow key in a folder selects "
"its first item, and a photograph is turned the way the camera held it. "
"Windows, tabs and dialogs let go of everything they held when they close."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:37
msgid ""
"A column view, the third way to look at a folder: the path drawn as a strip "
"of lists, one folder per column, with the folder you are in at the right and "
"whatever the selection points at beside it. One click in any other column "
"goes there. Ctrl+1, Ctrl+2 and Ctrl+3 now name a view instead of two keys "
"toggling. Shift and the wheel move the strip sideways, and a drag held near "
"either end pushes it along, so a column off the screen can still be dropped "
"on. A file written after it is created, an image pasted from the clipboard "
"say, gets its thumbnail without a restart."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:42
msgid ""
"A click on empty space in a folder takes the keyboard and clears the "
"selection, so Ctrl+A and the other file keys no longer wait for a file to be "
"clicked; the keyboard also comes back after a menu closes and after the "
"navigation buttons. A right click on empty space keeps the selection, and "
"the menu it opens acts on the folder. The search filters button has an icon "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:47
msgid ""
"Two folder panes side by side, off by default and turned on with F3: F6 "
"moves between them, the pane in charge is outlined, and everything outside "
"the view acts on that one. Dropping files asks whether to copy, move or "
"link, which Preferences can turn off. An up button beside back and forward. "
"\"Show in folder\" from a browser no longer waits twenty-five seconds on a "
"portal deadlock, and opens a window of its own with the file selected."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:52
msgid ""
"A new application icon. Files cut to the clipboard are faded until they are "
"pasted, and an image on the clipboard, a screenshot say, pastes into the "
"folder as a PNG. The clipboard keys work with the focus anywhere in the "
"window. Drags start anywhere on a row or grid tile and folders accept a drop "
"across their whole row. Compact, resizable list columns with the type shown "
"as the file extension, and a star toggle that follows the favourites."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:57
msgid ""
"Search walks subfolders, filters by type and date and can match file "
"contents. Visible columns and captions dialogs, expandable folders in the "
"list view. Restore from trash, links, Copy to and Move to, Run as a Program, "
"path bar and tab context menus, tabs moved between windows and restored "
"after closing. Password-protected archives. Lock emblems and greyed actions "
"for read-only files, folders that follow outside changes, and the clipboard "
"pastes paths into terminals."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:62
msgid ""
"Russian and Ukrainian translations. Sort order remembered per folder. A "
"Nautilus-style command line: new windows per call, -w, -s, -q. Filesystem "
"calls no longer block the interface on slow mounts."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.spiral.metainfo.xml:66
msgid "First release."
msgstr ""

